# ============================================
# Notes on Team Structure
# ============================================
#
# Replace team names with actual GitHub usernames or team references:
# - @guste                  - Primary maintainer
# - @platform-team          - Infrastructure platform engineers
# - @devops-team             - DevOps/SRE engineers
# - @devops-leads           - Senior DevOps engineers (required for prod changes)
# - @database-team          - Database specialists
# - @security-team          - Security engineers
# - @finops-team            - FinOps/cost optimization
# - @tech-docs-team         - Technical documentation team
# - @qa-team                - QA/Testing
#
# To use teams:
# 1. Create teams in GitHub: Settings → Teams → New Team
# 2. Add members to teams: Team → Members → Add member
# 3. Reference in CODEOWNERS as: @org/team-name
#
# Common patterns:
# - All: @username
# - Single file: /path/to/file.txt @username
# - Wildcard: /path/* @username
# - Multiple: /path/ @user1 @user2 (any can approve)
# - Extensions: *.tf @terraform-team
